FILE-01: write each [REPORT] field option once, including F-Factor

The [REPORT] writer loops over the fields below FRICTION. That range
includes the link quality field, which is also named "Quality" and is
always disabled, so every saved file has "Quality NO" after the node
quality line. The reader matches the node field, so the reloaded file
has no quality column. Skip the link quality field, which the reader
cannot address, and include FRICTION ("F-Factor"), which the reader
accepts but the writer left out.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply FILE-01_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/inpfile.c b/src/inpfile.c
index ad24244..a481af6 100644
--- a/src/inpfile.c
+++ b/src/inpfile.c
@@ -818,9 +818,12 @@ int saveinpfile(Project *pr, const char *fname)
     }
 
     // Field formatting options
-    for (i = 0; i < FRICTION; i++)
+    // (LINKQUAL is skipped: it has the same name as node QUALITY,
+    // which is the field the reader assigns that name to)
+    for (i = 0; i <= FRICTION; i++)
     {
         SField *field = &rpt->Field[i];
+        if (i == LINKQUAL) continue;
         if (field->Enabled == TRUE)
         {
             fprintf(f, "\n %-20sPRECISION %d", field->Name, field->Precision);
